    <bpmn:process id="W_W2674" name="W2674. Signage &amp; Billboard Permit Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening or signage replacement
Frequency: Per new store; ad-hoc replacements
Volume: 10–15 new stores; ~20–30 replacements/year
Owner: Facilities Manager
Participants: Facilities Mgr, Store Manager, LGU Engineering, Marketing
Source: workflow W2674 — Signage &amp; Billboard Permit Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W2674_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W2674_Lane1" name="Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2674_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2674_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W2674_Lane2" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2674_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2674_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2674_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W2674_Start4" name="New store opening or signage replacement">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2674_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2674_Task5" name="Marketing designs the signage per brand standards; Facilities ensures the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Marketing designs the signage per brand standards; Facilities ensures the design complies with the LGU sign ordinance (each LGU sets size limits, setback requirements, illumination restrictions, and Filipino-language requirements per the approved-national-language policy)
Responsible (R): Marketing / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): CMO / COO
Duration: Per project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2674_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2674_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2674_Task6" name="Facilities Manager obtains the sign permit from the LGU Engineering Office…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Facilities Manager obtains the sign permit from the LGU Engineering Office: submits the design, structural calculations (wind-load for large signs), electrical plan (for illuminated signs), building-owner consent where leased; pays the permit fee (PHP 5K–50K depending on size and LGU)
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 weeks before installation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2674_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2674_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2674_Task7" name="Signage contractor installs per the approved permit; LGU inspects…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Signage contractor installs per the approved permit; LGU inspects post-installation; Facilities maintains signage condition and ongoing compliance (illumination, structural integrity); tracks permit renewal where the LGU requires annual sign-permit renewal
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Contractor
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2674_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2674_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W2674_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W2674_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W2674_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-219: signage tracked as a maintained asset; operational: Facilities Manager sign-off that the permit is issued before the installation contractor mobilizes
Owner: Facilities Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
